as it turns out the most incredible and  over-the-top headquarters is not in the  states at all but far away on the other  side of the world in the outskirts of  seoul in south korea that's right today  i'll be talking about the samsung  digital city the home base of one of the  largest entities in the world how big it  is  first off let's just try and establish  the sheer scale of the thing so having  heard the word digital city i'm willing  to bet a lot of you guys are already so  having heard the word digital city i'm  willing to bet a lot of you guys are  already scoffing i mean it can't really  be anything close to a city right well i  certainly hope you're someone who can  change their opinions because at nearly  400 acres of space while it may not be a  metropolis it is still bigger than many  towns and by employing nearly 35 000  employees it certainly has a population  of one and honestly being the kind of  company it is samsung needs all the  space it can get because unlike their  other competitors companies like google  and apple samsung doesn't just deal in  one kind of product not to mention the  sheer volume of stuff they produce puts  the other companies to shame i mean  during 2019 in the span of just one  quarter the company managed to sell 71.9  million smartphone units nearly more  than the next two companies combined  with huawei and apple selling 59.1  million and 36.4 million each and that's  only scratching the surface because as  you should know by now while most of us  only know samsung as the gigantic  information technology and consumer  electronics maker that's not the only  thing they do by a large margin ventures  and companies just to mention a few of  their ventures their subsidiary samsung  heavy is the world's second largest  shipbuilding company while their  construction divisions samsung  engineering and samsung cnt are both two  of the largest construction companies  out there and it's not even just tech  that they're good at as companies like  samsung life insurance specialise in  more economic ventures and seeing as  they're the 14th largest insurance  company in the world they seem to be  good at that too so with all of that on  the table it's no secret that the 84  year old company needs a pretty  substantial place to do all those  activities from and that brings us to  the actual site of the headquarters in  the ancient city of suwon just 30  kilometers south of seoul south korea's  capital while the main site is located  there the company has since expanded  into neighbouring cities like yeongin  and huasung which all combine to form  the area known as the samsung digital  valley but for the sake of briefness and  general entertainment needs today i'll  only be focusing on the main site based  in suwon now as i mentioned earlier the  total area covered by samsung's campus  is nearly 400 square kilometers 390 to  be precise and that area alone puts it  above international sites like the  vatican or monaco and as it turns out  size is not the only thing that the  samsung digital city has in common with  those cities because as it turns out the  city that the headquarters sits upon has  a bit of old history you see with its  roots in the early 8th century the city  of suwon is actually the last completely  walled city in the entire country and  the fact that samsung chose it to be  their headquarters is not a coincidence  because one of the reasons that samsung  preferred su-1 instead of seoul was that  during the korean war the huge walls  surrounding suwon helped protect the  samsung facilities inside by comparison  huge bits of their sight in seoul were  severely damaged and having experienced  that and wanting to avoid any such  problems in the future the company's  founder libyong chul decided to  officially move the company headquarters  from the capital city to suwon in 1951  which would later turn out to be the  decision that led to everything that  exists in the city today which brings me  to the next part of our video now that  the history lesson is over what exactly  is on site now well this is where stuff  gets really interesting because while  yes the company has its fair share of  offices labs and other corporate staff  there is a lot more that goes into  making the various cogs and gears of  south korea's largest company run  smoothly towers  but first the basic stuff on the campus  by far the most prominent buildings are  the four 38-ish story tall towers which  house a lot of the office space for the  day-to-day workers but besides those  four there are a dozen or so smaller  towers and over 130 buildings that  include everything else from labs and  offices to recreational facilities like  cafes and clubs and besides all those  there is also a kindergarten school for  the children of company employees and  even a guest house for visiting  researchers now one of the most asked  questions about the site is regarding  its cost i mean if apple can splurge out  5 billion on a campus less than half the  size of samsung's how much would this  thing even cost well the answer here is  that it's complicated you see unlike the  apple park or the googleplex or any of  the other corporate headquarters that we  know of the samsung digital city was not  made in a span of a few years instead  the campus has been growing and  expanding ever since the company first  set foot here but just in case you're  still curious it's estimated that the  maintenance cost of the campus tops  multiple million dollars every single  year so to say that it was probably not  cheap would be an understatement now  that i'm done with all of that stuff we  can take a look at some of the details  that make up the daily life around the  campus and that's where the digital city  really shines because while all the  largest information companies do have at  least some benefits for their employees  samsung operates at such a larger scale  it's far more impressive to see them  make an effort for their employees and  what makes it even more impressive is  just how much of it is there because if  i'm being honest the experience of being  a samsung employee at the digital city  is not only excellent it might just be  the best one out there the experience  first up there are campus cafeterias  that's right cafeterias with an s and  not only are there dozens of them  scattered around the place but there are  also supposed to be over 100 menus  serving all kinds of food day in day out  and best of all you eat at these places  for absolutely free and just in case you  feel like the food is not up to your  standard you are also welcome to visit  the international food franchises also  found on campus like everyone's favorite  mcdonald's or dunkin donuts apart from  food and drink many many more benefits  come from working on site these include  free transport across the campus free  medical checkups with the on-site staff  in case you suffer an emergency and free  transport in case you need to go to a  different doctor there's a kindergarten  school we already mentioned as well as 9  000 or so umbrellas ready to be handed  out to employees in case of sudden rain  as far as attractions go the place has  plenty of them too most famous among  them is probably the samsung innovative  museum which unsurprisingly showcases  the 90s year history of the company  besides that there are weekly events  which include everything from rock  concerts to fashion and talk shows and  then there are the clubs which help  employees maintain an interest in  activities outside of work so that  whether you're someone who likes to  paint or has always wanted to paraglide  you don't have to blame work for not  letting you chase your passions and as  we all know fitness is an absolute  necessity for maximum productivity  especially at a company so reliant on  office work as samsung so there are  hundreds of sports clubs and over 10  basketball courts four badminton courts  three soccer fields two baseball  diamonds a climbing wall and an olympic  size swimming pool just in case you  thought anything was missing and then  there are more nerdy things like the  memo lab which secretly tests all of  samsung's products or the 5g city a  testing ground for new cellular and  wireless technologies i can go on and on  about all the awesome stuff that the  company has done for its employees but  what i find the most impressive is what  the company does for the people that  they're not directly responsible for  philanthropy and community service  you see for nearly 60 years since the  campus was founded samsung has  maintained a strong tradition of not  only giving locals access to its  healthcare and other services but by  directly supporting them as a customer  in the form of sourcing all the food  stuff locally and that i think is what  really sets this campus apart and in my  opinion makes it the most unique one on  earth i hope you enjoyed watching  today's video and if you did be sure to  leave a like and subscribe for more with  that take care and i'll see you guys  next time
 

